WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:08.480
One of the things I try to avoid on this show is&nbsp;
to be hyperbolic, and when people are going crazy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:13.520
about something and it's really no big deal, I&nbsp;
try to just say this is really not that big of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:18.800
deal. Let's talk about it, but let's talk about&nbsp;
it in sort of sober and reasonable terms. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:27.840
that is very much not the case when it comes to&nbsp;
the peril that is on the horizon. If Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:34.720
were to win the 2022 midterm elections in what are&nbsp;
just a few months now, quite frankly. And when I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:43.600
say democracy is in jeopardy if Republicans take&nbsp;
the House in 2022, I say it with the caveat that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:50.800
this is not a hyperbolic claim. And increasingly,&nbsp;
I mean, the bad thing is that democracy is in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.560
peril if Republicans win. The good thing is&nbsp;
increasingly people are understanding this

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:00.720
peril and this risk Republicans and Democrats who&nbsp;
are so similar on so many issues. We've talked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:05.840
about it before. Here's a whole bunch of issues&nbsp;
on which there's really no significant difference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:12.880
between Republicans and Democrats. How could it be&nbsp;
that if Republicans take one chamber of Congress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:20.560
it would have such a major impact, and the answer&nbsp;
is that it is because of the destructive potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.840
that the series of events that could be unleashed&nbsp;
by Republicans taking control of the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:32.240
is so significant that it could be the&nbsp;
catalyst for a disaster for democracy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:38.480
and let's just think it through. First, we&nbsp;
know that Republicans see their 2020 failure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:46.400
as a failure to steal the election. What I mean by&nbsp;
that is when you hear Republicans talk about 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.800
most of them, I mean, OK, Mitt Romney's the&nbsp;
exception. Liz Cheney is the exception. But for

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.840
the most part, when you hear Trump people&nbsp;
associated with the Trump White House, the more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.320
weaponized Republicans in the House and Senate,&nbsp;
when they talk about what happened in 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:08.000
their view is we. We just didn't do enough&nbsp;
to take the election from the guy who won&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.320
it. They don't think, you know, next time&nbsp;
we should really win by appealing to more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:16.480
voters and getting more people to vote for&nbsp;
us. That would be the normal reaction. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.240
would be the pro-democracy reaction. Not&nbsp;
enough. We didn't convince enough people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:26.320
let's be better at convincing people to vote for&nbsp;
us. No. They think we can win next time by better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.600
working to take the election, even when we don't&nbsp;
win it using different techniques or being better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:38.640
with the techniques that we used in 2022. But we&nbsp;
just didn't do enough of so. With a midterm 2020

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:43.120
to win, they would be far better to carry out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:51.040
upending of democracy in 2024. That's a very&nbsp;
dangerous thing. Secondly, Marjorie Taylor Greene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:03:00.720
Matt Gates and others in that cohort have said,&nbsp;
If we win in 2022, we are going to investigate Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.680
Biden. We're going to investigate Hunter Biden,&nbsp;
who has nothing to do with the administration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:11.440
We will end the January 6th committee. If it's&nbsp;
still going on, we will impeach Joe Biden and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:18.000
on and on and on. They've said that that's what&nbsp;
they're going to do disaster. And thirdly, they've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:27.200
said if they win, they will quickly work to&nbsp;
help the Trump rioters avoid consequences to any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:34.080
extent that they can, effectively rewarding the&nbsp;
rioters for what they did on January 6th of 2021.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:41.840
Now, in response to this, Nancy Pelosi, who I am&nbsp;
not a fan of Nancy Pelosi, recently said quote, It

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:48.400
is absolutely essential for our democracy that we&nbsp;
win. I fear for our democracy. If the Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.600
were ever to get the gavel, we can't let that&nbsp;
happen. And some people think she's being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:59.840
hyperbolic. But remember that Canadian political&nbsp;
scientist Thomas Homer Dixon, who we interviewed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:05.600
recently, he also wrote and explained to us during&nbsp;
the interview that the United States could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:11.760
under a right wing dictatorship by 2030. And when&nbsp;
I asked him what talk to us about the sequence?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:19.920
What are the initial steps and the precursor steps&nbsp;
to a right wing dictatorship in 2030 include Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:26.480
waiting in 2024, and a precursor to that would,&nbsp;
of course, be Republicans taking the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:33.600
in 2022. So the stakes are absolutely huge.&nbsp;
And if we just say what's most likely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.960
I'm not saying throw in the towel. I'm not&nbsp;
saying don't try. If anything, what I'm saying

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:44.640
is we've got to try. The more likely outcome,&nbsp;
even though Nancy Pelosi won't admit it, is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:50.320
Republicans take the House in 2022 if nothing&nbsp;
significant changes. Republicans only have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:55.520
flip five seats. Remember to take control of the&nbsp;
House in November. That's the most likely outcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:02.240
that they are able to flip at least five seats.&nbsp;
It is a very small margin of error for Democrats.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:08.880
Now the other aspect to all of this is, of course.&nbsp;
Is the Department of Justice going to act at all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:16.560
to show that what took place in 2020 simply cannot&nbsp;
happen again and truly hold people accountable? I,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:23.440
you know, I have no emotional investment in&nbsp;
Merrick Garland one way or the other. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.240
it's increasingly looking like Merrick Garland is&nbsp;
sort of spineless, and we're going to talk later

